-- Business days, public holidays and deadlines that roll (calendar library).
--
-- STATUS: draft (2026-10-24). specs/todo/ACT-TIME-GUARD-SPEC.md.
-- The library's function names were ruled on 2026-10-24 (card CAL).
--
-- A business-day clause can mean one of two things, and they are written
-- differently:
--
--   (a) the ACT must happen on a business day: "service may not be effected
--       on a Sunday or a public holiday". That is a condition on the act, a
--       PROVIDED. Today the act has to carry its own day for the PROVIDED to
--       read (§2-§5): no PROVIDED can read the time the act is stamped AT.
--
--   (b) the DEADLINE moves to a business day: "if the fifth day falls on a
--       Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, the next business day". That is a
--       computed anchor, `WITHIN 0 OF <the rolled day>` (§1, §6, §7).
--
-- They compose: §3 rolls the deadline AND guards the act.
--
-- Every trace here is stamped in date serials (`DATE_SERIAL`), the scale the
-- calendar library works on. In October and November 2026: Mon 26 Oct,
-- Fri 30 Oct, Sat 31 Oct, Mon 2 Nov, Tue 3 Nov, Thu 5 Nov, Fri 6 Nov.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT calendar

DECLARE Party IS ONE OF Seller, Buyer, Landlord, Tenant

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    notify        HAS day IS A NUMBER
    pay
    serve         HAS day IS A NUMBER
    deliver       HAS day IS A NUMBER
    lodge         HAS day IS A NUMBER
    `send notice` HAS day IS A NUMBER
    reply

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Wed 21 Oct` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 10 21)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Mon 26 Oct` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 10 26)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Thu 29 Oct` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 10 29)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Fri 30 Oct` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 10 30)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sat 31 Oct` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 10 31)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Mon 2 Nov` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 11 2)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Tue 3 Nov` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 11 3)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Wed 4 Nov` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 11 4)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Thu 5 Nov` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 11 5)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Fri 6 Nov` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 11 6)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Mon 9 Nov` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 11 9)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Mon 16 Nov` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 11 16)

#ASSERT `Weekday of` `Sat 31 Oct` EQUALS Saturday


-- §1 Reading (b): the deadline rolls. "The buyer shall pay within five days
-- of the notice; if the fifth day is not a business day, by the next business
-- day." Notice on Mon 26 Oct: the fifth day is Sat 31 Oct, which rolls to
-- Mon 2 Nov. Notice on Thu 29 Oct: the fifth day is Tue 3 Nov, a business
-- day, and nothing moves.

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Action
`pay within five days of notice, rolled` MEANS
    PARTY Seller MUST notify d WITHIN 10
    HENCE PARTY Buyer MUST pay WITHIN 0 OF (`next business day on or after` `weekdays only` (d PLUS 5))

-- rolled to Monday: paying on the Monday is in time
#TRACE `pay within five days of notice, rolled` AT `Mon 26 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Seller DOES notify `Mon 26 Oct` AT `Mon 26 Oct`
  PARTY Buyer DOES pay AT `Mon 2 Nov`

-- and the Tuesday is late
#TRACE `pay within five days of notice, rolled` AT `Mon 26 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Seller DOES notify `Mon 26 Oct` AT `Mon 26 Oct`
  PARTY Buyer DOES pay AT `Tue 3 Nov`

-- no roll: the fifth day is already a business day, so Tue 3 Nov is in time
#TRACE `pay within five days of notice, rolled` AT `Mon 26 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Seller DOES notify `Thu 29 Oct` AT `Thu 29 Oct`
  PARTY Buyer DOES pay AT `Tue 3 Nov`

-- and Wed 4 Nov is late: a business-day deadline is not pushed further
#TRACE `pay within five days of notice, rolled` AT `Mon 26 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Seller DOES notify `Thu 29 Oct` AT `Thu 29 Oct`
  PARTY Buyer DOES pay AT `Wed 4 Nov`


-- §2 Reading (a): the act must fall on a business day. "Service shall be
-- effected on a business day, within ten days." A PROVIDED that is FALSE
-- makes the act not count, and the next event is tried. The act carries its
-- own day, `d`, because no PROVIDED can read the act's AT stamp.

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Action
`serve on a business day within ten days` MEANS
    PARTY Landlord MUST serve d PROVIDED `is a business day` `weekdays only` d
    WITHIN 10

-- Saturday service does not count; Monday service, before Thu 5 Nov, does
#TRACE `serve on a business day within ten days` AT `Mon 26 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Landlord DOES serve `Sat 31 Oct` AT `Sat 31 Oct`
  PARTY Landlord DOES serve `Mon 2 Nov` AT `Mon 2 Nov`

-- Saturday service alone: the obligation is breached at its deadline
#TRACE `serve on a business day within ten days` AT `Mon 26 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Landlord DOES serve `Sat 31 Oct` AT `Sat 31 Oct`
  (`WAIT UNTIL` `Fri 6 Nov`)

-- THE GUARD DOES NOT MOVE THE DEADLINE. Started on Wed 21 Oct, ten days end
-- on Sat 31 Oct. The Saturday act is refused by the guard, and Monday is
-- after the deadline: breached. A business-day guard on the act and a
-- business-day roll of the deadline are two clauses, not one.
#TRACE `serve on a business day within ten days` AT `Wed 21 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Landlord DOES serve `Sat 31 Oct` AT `Sat 31 Oct`
  PARTY Landlord DOES serve `Mon 2 Nov` AT `Mon 2 Nov`


-- §3 (a) and (b) together: guard the act AND roll the deadline, so that the
-- last day of the window is a day on which the act can be done. The start is
-- passed in, because a top-level rule has no earlier act to count from.

GIVEN start IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Action
`serve on a business day within ten days, rolled` start MEANS
    PARTY Landlord MUST serve d PROVIDED `is a business day` `weekdays only` d
    WITHIN 0 OF (`next business day on or after` `weekdays only` (start PLUS 10))

-- the same Saturday and Monday as the last trace of §2: now in time
#TRACE (`serve on a business day within ten days, rolled` `Wed 21 Oct`) AT `Wed 21 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Landlord DOES serve `Sat 31 Oct` AT `Sat 31 Oct`
  PARTY Landlord DOES serve `Mon 2 Nov` AT `Mon 2 Nov`


-- §4 A KNOWN SILENT WRONG ANSWER, pinned so that a fix shows up here. The day
-- in the act is what the guard reads, and nothing checks it against the AT
-- stamp. Service stamped on Saturday but carrying Monday's day counts.
-- Only an act-time noun or binder would close this (spec §5, deferred).
#TRACE `serve on a business day within ten days` AT `Mon 26 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Landlord DOES serve `Mon 2 Nov` AT `Sat 31 Oct`


-- §5 A prohibition that applies only off business days: "no deliveries on a
-- Saturday, Sunday or public holiday". Friday delivery is not a violation;
-- Saturday delivery is.

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Action
`no deliveries off a business day` MEANS
    PARTY Seller SHANT deliver d PROVIDED NOT (`is a business day` `weekdays only` d)
    WITHIN 14

#TRACE `no deliveries off a business day` AT `Mon 26 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Seller DOES deliver `Fri 30 Oct` AT `Fri 30 Oct`
  (`WAIT UNTIL` `Mon 16 Nov`)

#TRACE `no deliveries off a business day` AT `Mon 26 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Seller DOES deliver `Sat 31 Oct` AT `Sat 31 Oct`


-- §6 "Provided it is not a public holiday", with the public holidays given as
-- a list of dates. This guard says nothing about weekends: a Saturday counts.
-- The list is an input of the rule, supplied where the rule is used.

GIVEN holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
      d        IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is one of the public holidays` holidays d MEANS
    elem (FLOOR d) (map Day holidays)

GIVEN holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Action
`lodge on a day that is not a public holiday` holidays MEANS
    PARTY Seller MUST lodge d PROVIDED NOT `is one of the public holidays` holidays d
    WITHIN 14

-- Mon 2 Nov is a public holiday: lodging then does not count, Tuesday does
#TRACE (`lodge on a day that is not a public holiday` (LIST YMD 2026 11 2)) AT `Mon 26 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Seller DOES lodge `Mon 2 Nov` AT `Mon 2 Nov`
  PARTY Seller DOES lodge `Tue 3 Nov` AT `Tue 3 Nov`

-- Mon 2 Nov alone: breached when the fourteen days run out
#TRACE (`lodge on a day that is not a public holiday` (LIST YMD 2026 11 2)) AT `Mon 26 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Seller DOES lodge `Mon 2 Nov` AT `Mon 2 Nov`
  (`WAIT UNTIL` `Mon 16 Nov`)

-- with no holidays listed, the same Monday counts
#TRACE (`lodge on a day that is not a public holiday` (EMPTY)) AT `Mon 26 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Seller DOES lodge `Mon 2 Nov` AT `Mon 2 Nov`

-- and a Saturday counts too, because it is not a public holiday
#TRACE (`lodge on a day that is not a public holiday` (LIST YMD 2026 11 2)) AT `Mon 26 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Seller DOES lodge `Sat 31 Oct` AT `Sat 31 Oct`


-- §7 A deadline that rolls over a weekend AND a public holiday to the next
-- business day. Notice on Mon 26 Oct; the fifth day, Sat 31 Oct, rolls past
-- the weekend and past the holiday on Mon 2 Nov to Tue 3 Nov.

GIVEN holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Action
`pay within five days of notice, rolled past holidays` holidays MEANS
    PARTY Seller MUST notify d WITHIN 10
    HENCE PARTY Buyer MUST pay
          WITHIN 0 OF (`next business day on or after` (`weekdays except the dates` holidays) (d PLUS 5))

-- with Mon 2 Nov a holiday, Tuesday is in time
#TRACE (`pay within five days of notice, rolled past holidays` (LIST YMD 2026 11 2)) AT `Mon 26 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Seller DOES notify `Mon 26 Oct` AT `Mon 26 Oct`
  PARTY Buyer DOES pay AT `Tue 3 Nov`

-- with no holiday listed, the same Tuesday is late
#TRACE (`pay within five days of notice, rolled past holidays` (EMPTY)) AT `Mon 26 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Seller DOES notify `Mon 26 Oct` AT `Mon 26 Oct`
  PARTY Buyer DOES pay AT `Tue 3 Nov`


-- §8 Deemed receipt: "a notice is deemed given on the business day after it
-- is sent; the landlord shall reply within three business days of receipt".
-- `add business days` by one is strictly after, so a notice sent on a business
-- day is deemed given on the next one, not the same day.

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Action
`reply within three business days of deemed receipt` MEANS
    PARTY Tenant MUST `send notice` d WITHIN 30
    HENCE PARTY Landlord MUST reply
          WITHIN 0 OF (`add business days` `weekdays only` 3 (`add business days` `weekdays only` 1 d))

-- sent Fri 30 Oct, deemed given Mon 2 Nov, reply due Thu 5 Nov
#TRACE `reply within three business days of deemed receipt` AT `Mon 26 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Tenant DOES `send notice` `Fri 30 Oct` AT `Fri 30 Oct`
  PARTY Landlord DOES reply AT `Thu 5 Nov`

#TRACE `reply within three business days of deemed receipt` AT `Mon 26 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Tenant DOES `send notice` `Fri 30 Oct` AT `Fri 30 Oct`
  PARTY Landlord DOES reply AT `Fri 6 Nov`

-- sent Mon 2 Nov, a business day: deemed given Tue 3 Nov, reply due Fri 6 Nov
#TRACE `reply within three business days of deemed receipt` AT `Mon 26 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Tenant DOES `send notice` `Mon 2 Nov` AT `Mon 2 Nov`
  PARTY Landlord DOES reply AT `Fri 6 Nov`


-- §9 The B1 spelling, `THE JOIN PLUS 5` in place of the day the act carries,
-- is in calendar-rollover-join.l4: it needs B1 (THE JOIN as a value), built
-- in part on lang/lifecycle-values (2026-10-24) and not merged to unstable,
-- so it is kept out of this file.
